---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Psychiatric Medication Management in Idaho | MWRS"
  description="Medication support for anxiety, depression, ADHD, and related concerns. In-person visits in Coeur d'Alene and Ponderay, with telehealth across Idaho."
>
  <main class="psychiatry-page">

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="subpage-hero">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <h1>Medication Management</h1>
        <p>
          MWRS offers thoughtful psychiatric medication management for adults
          and teens dealing with anxiety, depression, ADHD, and related
          concerns. Our psychiatric nurse practitioners (PMHNPs) provide
          careful, collaborative care with in-person visits in Coeur d'Alene
          and Ponderay, plus telehealth across Idaho.
        </p>
        <a href="/contact-us" class="btn-outline btn-outline--medication">
          Request a medication appointment
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- When medication may help -->
    <section class="psychiatry-body">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <h2>When medication may help</h2>
        <p>
          Medication is not the right fit for everyone, but it can be a helpful
          part of care when symptoms feel persistent, disruptive, or hard to
          manage through counseling alone.
        </p>
        <p>
          Some clients reach out because anxiety feels constant, depression is
          wearing them down, or focus and attention issues are affecting work,
          school, or daily life. Others simply want to talk through options with
          a prescriber and decide what makes sense.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our approach is thoughtful and collaborative. We take time to
          understand what has been going on, answer questions clearly, and
          consider whether medication fits your goals, preferences, and overall
          care.
        </p>

        <h3>Medication support may be worth considering for:</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Anxiety that feels difficult to settle</li>
          <li>Depression that is affecting daily life</li>
          <li>ADHD symptoms such as focus, organization, or follow-through</li>
          <li>Mood-related concerns that need further evaluation</li>
          <li>Situations where counseling alone has not felt like enough</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What to expect -->
    <section class="psychiatry-body psychiatry-body--light">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <h2>What to expect</h2>
        <p>
          The first appointment is a chance to talk through what has been going
          on, ask questions, and decide whether medication support makes sense
          for you. It is not a rushed or one-size-fits-all process.
        </p>

        <h3>At your first visit, we may talk about:</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Your current symptoms and how long they have been affecting you</li>
          <li>Past counseling, medication, or other treatment history</li>
          <li>Sleep, stress, focus, mood, and day-to-day functioning</li>
          <li>Your goals, preferences, and any concerns about medication</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          If medication seems like a good fit, your prescriber can talk through
          options, next steps, and follow-up care. If it does not, that is okay
          too. The goal is to find an approach that fits your needs.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Locations -->
    <section class="psychiatry-body">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <h2>Locations and availability</h2>
        <p>
          We offer medication management for adults and teens across Idaho, with
          both in-person and telehealth options.
        </p>

        <h3>In-person appointments</h3>
        <p>Available in Coeur d'Alene and Ponderay.</p>

        <h3>Telehealth</h3>
        <p>Available anywhere in Idaho through a secure video platform.</p>

        <p>
          Some clients prefer in-person visits, while others choose telehealth
          or a mix of both depending on their schedule and needs.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <section class="psychiatry-faq">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <h2 class="faq-heading">Common questions</h2>

        <div class="faq-list">
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              Do I have to take medication if I schedule an appointment?
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                No. The first visit is a conversation. You and your provider
                will talk through your symptoms, history, and goals, and decide
                together whether medication makes sense.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              Can I do both counseling and medication management?
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                Yes. Many clients use both. Medication can support symptom
                relief, while counseling helps address patterns, relationships,
                and long-term change.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              How often are follow-up appointments?
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                This depends on your situation. Some clients meet more
                frequently at the beginning and then space visits out once
                things are stable.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">Do you offer telehealth?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                Yes. We offer secure telehealth appointments for clients
                anywhere in Idaho, along with in-person visits in Coeur
                d'Alene and Ponderay.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">What conditions do you treat?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                We commonly help with anxiety, depression, ADHD, and related
                concerns, but each situation is unique. The first step is a
                conversation to understand what you are dealing with.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="psychiatry-cta">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <h2>Ready to talk through your options?</h2>
        <p>
          Whether you are looking for support with anxiety, depression, ADHD,
          or something less clear-cut, we can help you decide whether medication
          care makes sense for your situation.
        </p>
        <a href="/contact-us" class="btn-outline btn-outline--medication">
          Request a medication appointment
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

  <style>
    .psychiatry-page {
      background: #f9fafb;
      min-height: 100vh;
    }

    /* Override global lavender hero divider — sage on this page */
    :global(.subpage-hero) {
      border-bottom-color: #6a9e8e !important;
    }

    /* ── Hero ─────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .subpage-hero {
      padding: 10rem 1.5rem 3rem;
      background-color: #fbfbf9;
      background-image: url("/images/paper-texture.webp");
      background-repeat: repeat;
      background-size: 420px 420px;
      border-bottom: 3px solid #6a9e8e;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .subpage-hero h1 {
      font-family: "Belleza", sans-serif;
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 3vw, 2.6rem);
      letter-spacing: 0.16em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      margin: 0 0 1rem;
      color: #111827;
    }

    .subpage-hero p {
      margin: 0 0 1.6rem;
      font-size: 1rem;
      line-height: 1.8;
      color: #4b5563;
    }

    /* ── Shared section wrapper ───────────────────────── */
    .section-inner {
      max-width: 900px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    /* ── Body sections ────────────────────────────────── */
    .psychiatry-body {
      padding: 3rem 1.5rem 3.2rem;
      background-color: #e5e9f3;
      background-image: url("/images/paper-texture.webp");
      background-repeat: repeat;
      background-size: 420px 420px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.08);
    }

    .psychiatry-body--light {
      background-color: #fbfbf9;
    }

    .psychiatry-body h2 {
      font-family: "Belleza", sans-serif;
      font-size: 1.2rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.18em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      margin: 0 0 1rem;
      color: #111827;
    }

    .psychiatry-body h3 {
      margin: 1.5rem 0 0.4rem;
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: #111827;
    }

    .psychiatry-body p {
      margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
      font-size: 0.96rem;
      line-height: 1.8;
      color: #4b5563;
    }

    .psychiatry-body ul {
      margin: 0 0 1rem;
      padding-left: 1.1rem;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
      color: #4b5563;
    }

    .psychiatry-body li + li {
      margin-top: 0.2rem;
    }

    /* ── FAQ section ──────────────────────────────────── */
    .psychiatry-faq {
      padding: 3.5rem 1.5rem 4rem;
      background-color: #e5e9f3;
      background-image: url("/images/paper-texture.webp");
      background-repeat: repeat;
      background-size: 420px 420px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.08);
    }

    .faq-heading {
      font-family: "Belleza", sans-serif;
      font-size: 1.2rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.18em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      margin: 0 0 1.4rem;
      color: #111827;
    }

    .faq-list {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .faq-item {
      border-radius: 20px;
      background: #ffffff;
      border: 1.5px solid rgba(138, 180, 164, 0.5);
      box-shadow: 0 16px 40px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.08);
      padding: 1.1rem 1.4rem;
    }

    .faq-item summary {
      list-style: none;
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    .faq-item summary::-webkit-details-marker {
      display: none;
    }

    .faq-question {
      font-size: 0.98rem;
      font-weight: 500;
      color: #111827;
      margin: 0;
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0.75rem;
    }

    .faq-item summary::after {
      content: "+";
      font-size: 1.2rem;
      color: #8ab4a4;
      flex-shrink: 0;
      transition: color 0.15s ease;
    }

    .faq-item[open] summary::after {
      content: "–";
      color: #6a9e8e;
    }

    .faq-answer {
      margin-top: 0.6rem;
      font-size: 0.94rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
      color: #4b5563;
    }

    .faq-answer p {
      margin: 0;
    }

    /* ── CTA ──────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .psychiatry-cta {
      padding: 3rem 1.5rem 3.5rem;
      background-color: #fbfbf9;
      background-image: url("/images/paper-texture.webp");
      background-repeat: repeat;
      background-size: 420px 420px;
      border-top: 1px solid rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.06);
      text-align: center;
    }

    .psychiatry-cta h2 {
      font-family: "Belleza", sans-serif;
      font-size: 1.2rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.18em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      margin: 0 0 1rem;
      color: #111827;
    }

    .psychiatry-cta p {
      max-width: 620px;
      margin: 0 auto 1.6rem;
      font-size: 0.96rem;
      line-height: 1.8;
      color: #4b5563;
    }

    /* ── Outline button ───────────────────────────────── */
    .btn-outline {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: 0.85rem 1.9rem;
      border-radius: 999px;
      border: 1px solid;
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.14em;
      text-decoration: none;
      background: #ffffff;
      box-shadow: 0 6px 16px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.12);
      transition: background 0.15s ease, color 0.15s ease,
        box-shadow 0.15s ease, transform 0.15s ease;
    }

    .btn-outline--medication {
      border-color: #6a9e8e;
      color: #6a9e8e;
    }

    .btn-outline--medication:hover {
      background: #6a9e8e;
      color: #ffffff;
      transform: translateY(-1px);
      box-shadow: 0 10px 24px rgba(106, 158, 142, 0.3);
    }
  </style>
</Layout>